      "id": "@I70@",
      "name": "Rev Antoine Fleury",
      "gender": "M",
      "birth": "17 JUN 1705",
      "death": "6 APR 1801",
      "places": "Westminster, Middlesex, England, United Kingdom; Portarlington, County Laois, Ireland",
      "notes": "Antoine Fleury, was educated at Leyden, and on the 4th September, 1728, was ordained there. He came thence to London, and subsequently had charge of the French congregation, in the crypt under St. Patrick's. In 1761 he succeeded the Rev. Henry Gervaise, as one of the Vicars Choral of Lismore. His wife was of the noble De Rochebrune family.\n\nAnthony [Antoine] married Maria Julia Brunet in 1730.\n\nMarriage Licence\n\nFleury, Anthony, Rev, clerk and Maria Julia Brunet, parish St Peter, Dublin, spinster,. dated 22 June 1730\nAnthony [Antoine] married Elizabeth Foxcroft\n\nHe died in 1801\n\nProbate\n\nRev Anthony Fleury of Coolbanagher, Queen's county, clerk\nWill dated 21 February, proved 28 June 1801\nWife - Elizabeth Fleury, otherwise Foxcroft\nSon - John Charles Fleury, M.D.\nSon - George Charles [Louis] Fleury, Archdeacon of Waterford\nDaughter - Julia Maria Anna Dowdle\nDaughter - Elizabeth Morrison"
    },
